{title: Joyful, Joyful, We Adore Thee}
{artist: Henry van Dyke}
{key: G}
{tempo: 100}
{time: 4/4}
{meta: tune HYMN TO JOY - Ludwig van Beethoven (1824), arr. Edward Hodges (1864) (1864)}
{meta: public_domain Text 1907, tune 1864: both published before 1931 (US public domain); all authors, translators and composers died over 70 years ago. Chords and section layout: original simple arrangement by Tabernacle Tools. Original verses only, no modern additions.}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Joyful, joyful, [C]we a[G]dore Thee, [G]God of glory, [D]Lord of [G]love;
[G]Hearts unfold like [C]flowers be[G]fore Thee, [G]opening to the [D]sun a[G]bove.
[D]Melt the clouds of [G]sin and [D]sadness; [D]drive the dark of [G]doubt a[D]way;
[G]Giver of im[C]mortal [G]gladness, [G]fill us with the [D]light of [G]day!
{end_of_verse}
{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]All Thy works with [C]joy sur[G]round Thee, [G]earth and heaven re[D]flect Thy [G]rays,
[G]Stars and angels [C]sing a[G]round Thee, [G]center of un[D]broken [G]praise.
[D]Field and forest, [G]vale and [D]mountain, [D]flowery meadow, [G]flashing [D]sea,
[G]Singing bird and [C]flowing [G]fountain [G]call us to re[D]joice in [G]Thee.
{end_of_verse}
{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]Mortals, join the [C]happy [G]chorus, [G]which the morning [D]stars be[G]gan;
[G]Father love is [C]reigning [G]o'er us, [G]brother love binds [D]man to [G]man.
[D]Ever singing, [G]march we [D]onward, [D]victors in the [G]midst of [D]strife,
[G]Joyful music [C]leads us [G]sunward [G]in the triumph [D]song of [G]life.
{end_of_verse}
